═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
§ Apocky-blanket-authority decisions                                   D>
═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  D1 : Pike-VM over raw-NFA for regex engine
       ← bytecode-VM abstraction gives us feature-extensibility (future
         lookahead / atomic groups) without reshuffling state-table code
       ← RE2 precedent validates the choice
  D2 : UCD subset (L/N/P/S/Z/C) encoded as rune-ranges
       ← full UCD = 30 MB ; our subset = ~20 KB covers CSLv3 glyph usage
       ← binary search O(log n) per character
  D3 : lookahead / lookbehind deferred to v1.4.1
       ← clean NFA-only impl would need thread-scheduler extension
       ← current 38/38 selftest + Draft-07 wire-up sufficient for Session-15
       ← corpus doesn't require them yet
  D4 : `break step_loop` label for MATCH-thread exit
       ← Odin's `break` inside switch only exits switch, not enclosing
         for-loop ; documented in parser/DECISIONS.md Session-15 entry
  D5 : Alt compile uses split.x = left_start, split.y = right_start
       ← leftmost-first priority ; .x tried first by add_thread
       ← initial implementation had .y uninitialized (bug), fixed

